  "identifier": "finemed",
  "name": "FineMed",
  "alternateName": [
    "finemed-fr",
    "FineMed-fr French Medical Corpus"
  ],
  "description": "Large curated French medical pretraining corpus from Doctolib Lab — 21.1M documents and 19.2B words (81.6 GB) of real-world medical writing, assembled from FineWeb-2, FinePDFs, and FineWiki. Every document is labelled across three dimensions: medical subdomain (15 categories), educational quality (0–5), and medical-term density, enabling users to apply custom thresholds. Released unfiltered alongside a rephrased variant (finemed-rephrased-fr) in which an LLM rewrites documents into denser medical text. Produced via the data-curation recipe in the paper 'Where Does the Signal Live?' and used to pretrain the DoctoBERT encoder family. Three configs: fineweb-2 (18.9M docs), finepdfs (2.14M docs), finewiki (38.6k docs). Openly downloadable. Dual-licensed: fineweb-2 and finepdfs under ODC-BY-1.0; finewiki under CC-BY-SA-4.0.",
