  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "A substantial and openly licensed French medical pretraining corpus — 21.1M documents / 19.2B words with per-document annotations (subdomain, educational quality, medical-term density) that let users filter to their own thresholds, plus an LLM-rephrased dense variant. It fills a real gap in non-English open clinical NLP resources and is the verifiable training base for the DoctoBERT encoders, which strengthens its provenance. Marked Assess rather than Adopt for two reasons. (1) Licensing is a genuine consumer trap: the corpus is dual-licensed — ODC-BY-1.0 for the fineweb-2 and finepdfs configs, CC-BY-SA-4.0 for finewiki — and is derived from upstream web sources, so downstream users must honour the per-config terms (the share-alike clause on finewiki in particular propagates to derivatives). (2) It is web-derived medical text, not clinically validated or de-identified clinical records, so quality and safety for any clinical use must be assessed by the user. Valuable now for teams training French medical language models who can comply with the per-config licences. Companion model cataloged separately as doctobert (ai-ml-models).",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-24",
